        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0315" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg143"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 857.857/81</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Havre</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Osborne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Havre</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 23, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received midnight.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Norwegian steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Alice</hi>, unarmed, no passengers,
                    carrying coal Port Albert to Tréport, cannonaded without warning by enemy
                    submarine, nationality unknown, off Fécamp, February 21. More than 20 shots
                    fired, imperilling crew 14 including Theo Joseph, American
                    negro, born Fernandina, Fla. <hi rendition="#italic">Alice</hi> then sunk by
                    bombs. Depositions Norwegian captain and Joseph taken.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Osborne</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
